    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOKIsnqM8AAAABNH7J7w",
      "title": "eth/089: OP Mainnet unsafe block signer renumber (088 → 089) and FUS nonce re-pin (84 → 85)",
      "author": "Wazabie",
      "number": 1613,
      "body": "Renumbers the OP Mainnet unsafe block signer task to **eth/089** and moves it to FoundationUpgradeSafe nonce **85**, after U21 and the Soneium Mainnet tasks.\n\n## Change\n\n| | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Task | `eth/088-op-mainnet-set-unsafe-signer` | `eth/089-op-mainnet-set-unsafe-signer` |\n| FoundationUpgradeSafe nonce | 84 | **85** |\n| Message hash | `0xe001da1e…0414b` | **`0xb091d40b179d6d63ae01adeea4d6c3e460e2aaf748603a0016e1ef62271af1f8`** |\n| Calldata | — | unchanged |\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> Anyone who signed the old eth/088 at nonce 84 must re-sign.\n\n## Why\n\nU21 (eth/084) took nonce 81, which moved the Soneium tasks (#1566) to 82–84. Nonce 84 then collided with eth/087, and the stacked simulation failed. The new number frees eth/088 for the Soneium rollback (#1588).\n\n## FoundationUpgradeSafe sequence\n\n| Nonce | Task | PR |\n|---|---|---|\n| 81 | eth/084 U21 | main |\n| 82 | eth/085 Soneium proposer | #1566 |\n| 83 | eth/086 Soneium batcher and unsafe signer | #1566 |\n| 84 | eth/087 Soneium fee vaults, *or* eth/088 rollback | #1566 / #1588 |\n| **85** | **eth/089 OP Mainnet unsafe signer** | **this PR** |\n\n## Verification\n\n`just simulate-stack eth 089-op-mainnet-set-unsafe-signer` passes on this branch and with #1566 stacked on top, with the same hash.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops",
      "createdAt": "2026-11-05T17:18:17Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-11-09T18:26:32Z",
      "additions": 709,
      "deletions": 13
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOKIsnqM8AAAABGEfZxA",
      "title": "sep/115-117: Soneium Minato migration tasks",
      "author": "Wazabie",
      "number": 1565,
      "body": "The Soneium Minato migration ceremony in two tasks, same shape as Unichain Sepolia (#1563). sep/115 sets the OP Enterprise batcher and unsafe block signer (cutover steps 2 and 3), signed by the Sepolia FoundationUpgradeSafe, which becomes the SystemConfig owner with sep/111 (#1561). sep/116 rotates the `SUPER_PERMISSIONED` (5) proposer (cutover step 4), signed by the L1PAO; Minato's respected game stays `SUPER_CANNON_KONA` (9), so type 5 is the fallback, and post-U20 there is no challenger to rotate.\n\nsep/117 moves the L1FeeVault and OperatorFeeVault to the OPE cost recipient on L1 with a 0.15 ETH minimum (eth/062 values; L1FeeVault already withdraws to L1, so 5 deposits), signed by the L1PAO and stacked after sep/116 (L1PAO 60 / FUS 82 / SC 74). The Sequencer and Base vaults stay on Sony's L1 Safe `0x7CE93e2bEa4D52e7d7C6870F294874ef034C31Cd`. The cost recipient is the `0xdead…1004` placeholder.\n\nThe OPE batcher, sequencer and proposer are `0xdead…1001` to `…1003` placeholders, so both tasks are DRAFT. Stacked on #1563 because the FoundationUpgradeSafe, L1PAO and Security Council nonces follow sep/112-114: sep/115 FUS 80, sep/116 L1PAO 59 / FUS 81 / SC 73 (live 2026-10-01: 57 / 77 / 71). Minato cuts over after U21 Sepolia: once the U21 tasks exist, these pins and hashes move, the tasks may need renumbering after them, and if U21 redeploys the type-5 game the impl changes too. Calldata was re-derived independently with `cast`, and `just simulate-stack` passes on both signing paths.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-01T10:17:49Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-11-09T18:26:32Z",
      "additions": 702,
      "deletions": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOKIsnqM8AAAABGEi1SQ",
      "title": "eth/081-083: Soneium Mainnet migration tasks",
      "author": "Wazabie",
      "number": 1566,
      "body": "The Soneium Mainnet migration ceremony in two tasks, same shape as Minato (#1565). eth/081 sets the OP Enterprise batcher and unsafe block signer (cutover steps 2 and 3), signed by the FoundationUpgradeSafe, which becomes the SystemConfig owner with eth/075 (#1561). eth/082 rotates the `SUPER_PERMISSIONED` (5) proposer (cutover step 4), signed by the L1PAO. On Soneium Mainnet type 5 is the respected and only game type (no type 9), so this rotation is blocking for the cutover; post-U20 there is no challenger to rotate.\n\neth/083 moves the L1FeeVault and OperatorFeeVault from Sony's Safe `0x34ffF1A1CB3C054E9eD1BbD36883B14A66E6C260` (set by eth/072) to the OPE cost recipient on L1 with a 0.15 ETH minimum (eth/062 values, 6 deposits), signed by the L1PAO and stacked after eth/082 (L1PAO 48 / FUS 79 / SC 75). The Sequencer and Base vaults stay on Sony's Safe. The cost recipient is the `0xdead…1004` placeholder.\n\nThe OPE batcher, sequencer and proposer are `0xdead…1001` to `…1003` placeholders, so both tasks are DRAFT; eth/082 also needs the Maintenance Upgrade governance post. Stacked on #1564 because the FoundationUpgradeSafe, L1PAO and Security Council nonces follow eth/077-080: eth/081 FUS 77, eth/082 L1PAO 47 / FUS 78 / SC 74 (live 2026-10-01: 44 / 73 / 71). Soneium cuts over after U21 Mainnet: once the U21 tasks exist, these pins and hashes move, the tasks may need renumbering after them, and if U21 redeploys the type-5 game the impl changes too. Calldata was re-derived independently with `cast`, and `just simulate-stack` passes on both signing paths.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-01T10:23:33Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-11-09T17:59:58Z",
      "additions": 696,
      "deletions": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOKIsnqM8AAAABOHpZXg",
      "title": "ci: add agent approval check",
      "author": "falcorocks",
      "number": 1617,
      "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds an `agent-approval-check` workflow that calls the reusable ethereum-optimism/factory `.github/workflows/agent-approval-check.yaml`, pinned to ethereum-optimism/factory@feec17f6a55c3bd2dd1f0f0459e942688489222f. It reports the `agent-approval-check` commit status on pull requests, reviews, `/approve` comments and merge groups. Pull requests authored by, approved by, or containing commits from agent and automation identities stay pending until two distinct human reviewers with write access approve the current head.\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops",
      "createdAt": "2026-11-10T13:56:03Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-11-10T16:27:12Z",
